      "id": "IMI-02",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-isogeny-finite-specializations",
      "title": "Finitely many target specializations in both directions",
      "hypotheses": "The hypotheses of the elementary correspondence hold: finite étale maps over X[1/q], a polarized isogeny of multiplier c = q^n with companion, the multiplicity-one Lie condition, embeddings distinct modulo q, q not dividing tr² − 4nm, and level N ≥ 3 prime to q.",
      "statement": "For a fixed point u of X, the closed points of the target extensions of all valuative tests starting at u form a finite set. The same holds for the sources of tests ending at a fixed point.",
      "definitions": [
        "A valuative test is a discrete valuation ring V with a point x of Y₀ over its fraction field and V-points extending s₀(x) and t₀(x)."
      ],
